                        Release v1.2.22 for VSCode with config.yaml fixes, dependency updates, and session history filtering improvements.\n   298→                    </div>\n   299→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   300→                        <span class=\"meta-tag update-type-release\">release</span>\n   301→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">VSCode</span>\n   302→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">2026-03-27</span>\n   303→                    </div>\n   304→                </div>\n   305→\n   306→                <div class=\"item\">\n   307→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   308→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases/tag/v1.0.67-jetbrains\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n   309→                            Continue v1.0.67\n   310→                        </a>\n   311→                    </div>\n   312→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   313→                        Release v1.0.67 for JetBrains with IPC stream corruption fixes, config.yaml improvements, and dependency updates.\n   314→                    </div>\n   315→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   316→                        <span class=\"meta-tag update-type-release\">release</span>\n   317→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">JetBrains</span>\n   318→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">2026-03-27</span>\n   319→                    </div>\n   320→                </div>\n   321→\n   322→                <div class=\"item\">\n   323→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   324→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases/tag/v1.3.37-vscode\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n   325→                            Continue v1.3.37\n   326→                        </a>\n   327→                    </div>\n   328→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   329→                        Removed Ollama template-based tool support gate in v1.3.37 for VSCode.\n   330→                    </div>\n   331→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   332→                        <span class=\"meta-tag update-type-bugfix\">bugfix</span>\n   333→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">VSCode</span>\n   334→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">2026-03-26</span>\n   335→                    </div>\n   336→                </div>\n   337→\n   338→                <div class=\"item\">\n   339→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   340→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases/tag/v1.3.36-vscode\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n   341→                            Continue v1.3.36\n   342→                        </a>\n   343→                    </div>\n   344→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   345→                        Comprehensive bug fix release addressing crashes, security vulnerabilities, memory leaks, and JetBrains freezes. Includes new ClawRouter provider for cost-optimized model routing.\n   346→                    </div>\n   347→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   348→                        <span class=\"meta-tag update-type-bugfix\">bugfix</span>\n   349→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">VSCode</span>\n   350→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">2026-03-26</span>\n   351→                    </div>\n   352→                </div>\n   353→\n   354→                <div class=\"item\">\n   355→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   356→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases/tag/v1.3.35-vscode\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n   357→                            Continue v1.3.35\n   358→                        </a>\n   359→                    </div>\n   360→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   361→                        Extensive updates including support for reasoning_content field, Responses API opt-out, multiple provider fixes (Ollama, vLLM, OpenRouter), and Gemini 3 tool support.\n   362→                    </div>\n   363→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   364→                        <span class=\"meta-tag update-type-feature\">feature</span>\n   365→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">VSCode</span>\n   366→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">2026-03-26</span>\n   367→                    </div>\n   368→                </div>\n   369→            </section>\n   370→\n   371→            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   372→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   373→                <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n   374→\n   375→                <div class=\"item\">\n   376→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   377→                        <span class=\"highlight\">Web Search Tools Rate Limited</span>\n   378→                    </div>\n   379→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   380→                        All web search and web reader tools (WebSearch, webReader) have reached their weekly/monthly rate limits. The tools report: <code>'Weekly/Monthly Limit Exhausted. Your limit will reset at 2026-04-09 11:47:49'</code>. Without access to external sources, I cannot fetch fresh insights from thought leaders, blogs, YouTube, podcasts, or community platforms for the date range 2026-03-27 to 2026-04-03.\n   381→                    </div>\n   382→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   383→                        <span class=\"meta-tag system\">system</span>\n   384→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">rate-limit</span>\n   385→                        <span class=\"meta-tag\">unavailable</span>\n   386→                    </div>\n   387→                </div>\n   388→            </section>\n   389→        </main>\n   390→\n   391→        <footer>\n   392→            <a href=\"#\">Top</a>\n   393→ 